{% column %}
Mobility means **moving from one place to another**.

You can walk or use a wheelchair.

You can take a bus or a train.

Travelling on your own makes you **more independent**.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}
{% /slide %}

{% slide align="center" hideNavigation=false %}
{% columns %}
{% column %}
{% arasaac #24296 alt="Map" size=300 /%}
{% /column %}

{% column %}
Many people use AI on their phone to travel.

AI can help you find the way.

AI can also make mistakes.

A mistake can make you go on the wrong place.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}
{% /slide %}

{% slide align="center" hideNavigation=false %}
{% columns %}
{% column %}
{% arasaac #39705 alt="AI" size=300 /%}
{% /column %}

{% column %}
In this module you learn:

- You can ask an AI assistant about your trip.
- A good question has the **need**, the **place** and the **time**.
- You check important answers in a second place.
- Your home address is private.
{% /column %}
{% /columns %}
{% /slide %}
{% /slideshow %}
